  "id": "reversal-theory",
  "term": "reversal theory",
  "definition": "Reversal theory is a psychological approach that explains behaviour in terms of shifts, or reversals, between meta-motivational states. In this packet, it is used to describe how changes in motivational state can alter priorities and contribute to sudden unsanctioned aggression under pressure.",
